You: **Very concerned.** Astemizole is an established, potent hERG blocker, so the ToxPred “blocker” call (0.80 versus its 0.41 threshold) agrees with experimental evidence. A patch clamp study measured an hERG IC₅₀ of **0.9 nM** for astemizole and **1.0 nM** for its major metabolite, desmethylastemizole. The metabolite persists and can dominate circulating exposure. [Zhou et al.](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10376921/)

